---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.svg";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A diagram in the course's own vocabulary: a record track running unbroken while a capability track stops, then resumes at a visible cost"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Twelve seminars, each built around one documented case of an institution
    finding out it had lost something it thought it still had — from a
    laser nobody could rebuild from the published papers, to a nuclear
    material a production line could no longer remake from its own surviving
    paperwork. For each case you'll apply a small, consistent method: pull
    apart the record of a practice from the capability to actually perform
    it, and locate exactly where, if anywhere, the two came apart. You'll
    run that method on a case of your own for the case dossier, test it on
    yourself with the reproduction attempt, and use it to argue a position
    of your own in the seminar paper — including, if you choose, on the
    live and unresolved case in week 11.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who can read a documented historical or organisational case
    closely and argue from it — no engineering, materials science, or
    technical background is assumed, and week 4's case is deliberately kept
    at the level of institutional history rather than technical detail. If
    "we have the manual, so we still know how" is a sentence you've never
    had reason to doubt, this course is aimed at you.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The twelve weekly cases, in order, starting with the distinction the whole course rests on.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>Three pieces of work, weighted 30/25/45, all built on the same method.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Glossary" href="/glossary/">
      <p>Every term the course relies on, defined once and linked from every week that uses it.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
